{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107402","id":2584021340,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6aBQlc","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107402","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107402.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107402.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107402","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107402/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107402/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107402/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d160d717969bfcaf0f1dd17de9e8c9ec54a6db0b","number":107402,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Stop `FileAccess::fix_path` from emitting errors for invalid UIDs","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #101962.\r\n\r\nThis is mostly a quick hack to prompt a discussion about a more proper fix, and maybe serve as a hold-over, but...\r\n\r\nThis adds a `ResourceUID::has_id` check to `FileAccess::fix_path`, before it tries to call `ResourceUID::text_to_id`, and instead just clears the output string if it's not a known UID, same as what this error check is already doing inadvertently by returning an empty `String` when it can't find the UID:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/51b0379e5502402d44818a4b6f301f544a5754f3/core/io/resource_uid.cpp#L199\r\n\r\nWithout this, you could otherwise pass perfectly reasonable (or not) but non-existent `uid://` paths to `FileAccess::fix_path` and it would emit the above mentioned error about `Unrecognized UID`, which is exactly what happens in places like the LSP server, where it runs every string literal in the GDScript file through `FileAccess::file_exists`, which in turn calls `FileAccess::fix_path`, as seen here:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/51b0379e5502402d44818a4b6f301f544a5754f3/modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_extend_parser.cpp#L207-L214\r\n\r\nI feel like the proper fix is to change `FileAccess::fix_path` to instead return a `bool`, to indicate a failure to fix/resolve the path, like when trying to fix/resolve a non-existent UID, but since that would/should require changing quite a lot of call sites I settled for this for now.\r\n\r\nThe fact that the LSP server is running every GDScript string literal through `FileAccess::file_exists` is maybe a bit questionable as well, but that seems like more of a performance concern than anything else. `FileAccess::file_exists` should not throw errors on non-existent UIDs.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","descripti